IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, section 114 (piece dg1): application of the chapter to
-- nonstock corporations. Layer 1: the law, objectively; nobody's point of view.
--
-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, a plain-text rendering of the Delaware Code Online, not the
-- official text. `-- src:N | ...` is a slice of line N; an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- Subsection (d) decides which of the core's four `Kind of corporation` a corporation is; every other piece takes
-- that kind as a plain input. Subsections (b) and (c) are carried as data: the sections, parts of sections and
-- subchapters to which the stockholder-to-member reading does not apply.
-- Sections 503 and 502(a)(5) belong to chapter 5 of this title, which is not among the inputs; they are carried as
-- numbers in the lists, because the text lists them.

§ `Section 114 -- Application of chapter to nonstock corporations`

§§ `s 114 Provisions named in the lists`

-- A provision is a section of this title, or a named part of one ("102(a)(4)", "109(b) (last sentence)"). A part is
-- written as the text writes it, at the level at which the lists name it; an empty subdivision names the whole
-- section.
-- src:201 | (1) Sections 102(a)(4), (b)(1) and (2), 109(a), 114, 141, 154, 215, 228, 230(b), 241, 242, 253, 254, 255, 256, 257, 258, 271, 276, 311, 312, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(b)(1) (src:201)
DECLARE `s 114 Provision` HAS
    section                                                                                    IS A NUMBER
    subdivision                                                                                IS A STRING

-- src:203 | (3) Subchapter XIV and subchapter XVI of this chapter.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(b)(3) (src:203)
DECLARE `s 114 Subchapter` HAS
    `first section`                                                                            IS A NUMBER
    `last section`                                                                             IS A NUMBER

-- src:201 | (1) Sections 102(a)(4), (b)(1) and (2), 109(a), 114, 141, 154, 215, 228, 230(b), 241, 242, 253, 254, 255, 256, 257, 258, 271, 276, 311, 312, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(b)(1) (src:201)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 114 Provision`
`s 114 the whole of section` n MEANS `s 114 Provision` WITH section IS n, subdivision IS ""

-- src:201 | (1) Sections 102(a)(4), (b)(1) and (2), 109(a), 114, 141, 154, 215, 228, 230(b), 241, 242, 253, 254, 255, 256, 257, 258, 271, 276, 311, 312, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(b)(1) (src:201)
GIVEN part IS A STRING
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 114 Provision`
`s 114 the part` part `of section` n MEANS `s 114 Provision` WITH section IS n, subdivision IS part

