-- A listed provision names the asked provision if it is the same section and either names the whole section or the
-- same part.
-- src:201 | (1) Sections 102(a)(4), (b)(1) and (2), 109(a), 114, 141, 154, 215, 228, 230(b), 241, 242, 253, 254, 255, 256, 257, 258, 271, 276, 311, 312, 313, 390, and 503 of this title, which apply to nonstock corporations by their terms;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(b)(1) (src:201)
GIVEN listed IS A `s 114 Provision`
      asked IS A `s 114 Provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 114 the listed provision names the asked provision` listed asked MEANS
        (listed's section EQUALS asked's section)
    AND (   listed's subdivision EQUALS ""
         OR listed's subdivision EQUALS asked's subdivision)

-- src:201 | (1) Sections 102(a)(4), (b)(1) and (2), 109(a), 114, 141, 154, 215, 228, 230(b), 241, 242, 253, 254, 255, 256, 257, 258, 271, 276, 311, 312, 313, 390, and 503 of this title, which apply to nonstock corporations by their terms;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(b)(1) (src:201)
GIVEN list IS A LIST OF `s 114 Provision`
      asked IS A `s 114 Provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 114 the list names the provision` list asked MEANS
    any (GIVEN listed YIELD `s 114 the listed provision names the asked provision` listed asked) list

-- src:203 | (3) Subchapter XIV and subchapter XVI of this chapter.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(b)(3) (src:203)
GIVEN list IS A LIST OF `s 114 Subchapter`
      asked IS A `s 114 Provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 114 the list of subchapters reaches the provision` list asked MEANS
    any (GIVEN range YIELD (asked's section AT LEAST range's `first section`) AND (asked's section AT MOST range's `last section`)) list

§§ `s 114(a) to (c) The reading of references`

-- src:195 | (a) Except as otherwise provided in subsections (b) and (c) of this section, the provisions of this chapter and of chapter 5 of this title shall apply to nonstock corporations in the manner specified in the following paragraphs (a)(1)-(4) of this section:
-- src:196 | (1) All references to stockholders of the corporation shall be deemed to refer to members of the corporation;
-- src:197 | (2) All references to the board of directors of the corporation shall be deemed to refer to the governing body of the corporation;
-- src:198 | (3) All references to directors or to members of the board of directors of the corporation shall be deemed to refer to members of the governing body of the corporation; and
-- src:199 | (4) All references to stock, capital stock, or shares thereof of a corporation authorized to issue capital stock shall be deemed to refer to memberships of a nonprofit nonstock corporation and to membership interests of any other nonstock corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(a) (src:195-199)
DECLARE `s 114(a) Kind of reference` IS ONE OF
    `a reference to stockholders of the corporation`
    `a reference to the board of directors of the corporation`
    `a reference to directors or to members of the board of directors of the corporation`
    `a reference to stock, capital stock, or shares thereof of a corporation authorized to issue capital stock`

-- src:195 | (a) Except as otherwise provided in subsections (b) and (c) of this section, the provisions of this chapter and of chapter 5 of this title shall apply to nonstock corporations in the manner specified in the following paragraphs (a)(1)-(4) of this section:
-- src:196 | (1) All references to stockholders of the corporation shall be deemed to refer to members of the corporation;
-- src:197 | (2) All references to the board of directors of the corporation shall be deemed to refer to the governing body of the corporation;
-- src:198 | (3) All references to directors or to members of the board of directors of the corporation shall be deemed to refer to members of the governing body of the corporation; and
-- src:199 | (4) All references to stock, capital stock, or shares thereof of a corporation authorized to issue capital stock shall be deemed to refer to memberships of a nonprofit nonstock corporation and to membership interests of any other nonstock corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(a) (src:195-199)
DECLARE `s 114(a) Reading` IS ONE OF
    `as written`
    `as a reference to members of the corporation`
    `as a reference to the governing body of the corporation`
    `as a reference to members of the governing body of the corporation`
    `as a reference to memberships of a nonprofit nonstock corporation`
    `as a reference to membership interests of a nonstock corporation that is not a nonprofit nonstock corporation`

-- Subsection (b): (a) does not apply to the (b)(1) sections, the (b)(2) sections, and subchapters XIV and XVI.
-- Subsection (c): for a nonprofit nonstock corporation it does not apply to those, nor to the (c)(2) sections, nor to
-- the (c)(3) subchapters (subchapter V, subchapter VI other than sections 204 and 205, and subchapter XV).
-- src:200 | (b) Subsection (a) of this section shall not apply to:
-- src:201 | (1) Sections 102(a)(4), (b)(1) and (2), 109(a), 114, 141, 154, 215, 228, 230(b), 241, 242, 253, 254, 255, 256, 257, 258, 271, 276, 311, 312, …
-- src:202 | (2) Sections 102(f), 109(b) (last sentence), 151, 152, 153, 155, 156, 157(e), 158, 161, 162, 163, 164, 165, 166, 167, …
-- src:203 | (3) Subchapter XIV and subchapter XVI of this chapter.
-- src:204 | (c) In the case of a nonprofit nonstock corporation, subsection (a) of this section shall not apply to:
-- src:205 | (1) The sections and subchapters listed in subsection (b) of this section;
-- src:206 | (2) Sections 102(b)(3), 111(a)(2) and (3), 144(a)(2), 217, 218(a) and (b), and 262 of this title; and
-- src:207 | (3) Subchapter V, subchapter VI (other than §§ 204 and 205 of this title) and subchapter XV of this chapter.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(b), (c) (src:200-207)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
      asked IS A `s 114 Provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 114(b) and (c) subsection (a) does not apply to the provision` kind asked MEANS
        `s 114 the list names the provision` (`s 114(b)(1) the provisions that apply to nonstock corporations by their terms`) asked
     OR `s 114 the list names the provision` (`s 114(b)(2) the other provisions to which subsection (a) does not apply`) asked
     OR `s 114 the list of subchapters reaches the provision` (`s 114(b)(3) the subchapters to which subsection (a) does not apply`) asked
     OR (    `the kind is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` kind
         AND (   `s 114 the list names the provision` (`s 114(c)(2) the further provisions to which subsection (a) does not apply for a nonprofit nonstock corporation`) asked
              OR `s 114 the list of subchapters reaches the provision` (`s 114(c)(3) the subchapters to which subsection (a) does not apply for a nonprofit nonstock corporation`) asked
              -- sections 204 and 205 are carved out of the subchapter VI exclusion (the list stops at section 203)
              ))

-- Except as subsections (b) and (c) provide, the provisions of this chapter (and of chapter 5) apply to nonstock
-- corporations as the paragraphs (a)(1)-(4) specify: stockholders are read as members, the board of directors as
-- the governing body, directors or members of the board as members of the governing body, and stock, capital stock
-- or shares as memberships of a nonprofit nonstock corporation and membership interests of any other nonstock
-- corporation. A stock corporation's references are read as written.
-- src:195 | (a) Except as otherwise provided in subsections (b) and (c) of this section, the provisions of this chapter and of chapter 5 of this title shall apply to nonstock corporations in the manner specified in the following paragraphs (a)(1)-(4) of this section:
-- src:196 | (1) All references to stockholders of the corporation shall be deemed to refer to members of the corporation;
-- src:197 | (2) All references to the board of directors of the corporation shall be deemed to refer to the governing body of the corporation;
-- src:198 | (3) All references to directors or to members of the board of directors of the corporation shall be deemed to refer to members of the governing body of the corporation; and
-- src:199 | (4) All references to stock, capital stock, or shares thereof of a corporation authorized to issue capital stock shall be deemed to refer to memberships of a nonprofit nonstock corporation and to membership interests of any other nonstock corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(a) (src:195-199)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
      asked IS A `s 114 Provision`
      reference IS A `s 114(a) Kind of reference`
GIVETH A `s 114(a) Reading`
`s 114(a) how the reference in the provision is read` kind asked reference MEANS
    IF (`the kind is a stock corporation` kind) OR `s 114(b) and (c) subsection (a) does not apply to the provision` kind asked
    THEN `as written`
    ELSE CONSIDER reference
         WHEN `a reference to stockholders of the corporation` THEN `as a reference to members of the corporation`
         WHEN `a reference to the board of directors of the corporation` THEN `as a reference to the governing body of the corporation`
         WHEN `a reference to directors or to members of the board of directors of the corporation` THEN `as a reference to members of the governing body of the corporation`
         WHEN `a reference to stock, capital stock, or shares thereof of a corporation authorized to issue capital stock` THEN
             IF `the kind is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` kind
             THEN `as a reference to memberships of a nonprofit nonstock corporation`
             ELSE `as a reference to membership interests of a nonstock corporation that is not a nonprofit nonstock corporation`

§§ `s 114(d) Definitions`

-- A "nonstock corporation" is any corporation organized under this chapter that is not authorized to issue capital
-- stock.
-- src:212 | (4) A “nonstock corporation” is any corporation organized under this chapter that is not authorized to issue capital stock.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(d)(4) (src:212)
GIVEN `the corporation is organized under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is authorized to issue capital stock` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 114(d)(4) the corporation is a nonstock corporation` `the corporation is organized under this chapter` `the corporation is authorized to issue capital stock` MEANS
        `the corporation is organized under this chapter`
    AND (NOT (`the corporation is authorized to issue capital stock`))

-- A "membership interest" is, unless otherwise provided in a nonstock corporation's certificate of incorporation, a
-- member's share of the profits and losses of a nonstock corporation, or a member's right to receive distributions of
-- its assets, or both.
-- src:210 | (2) A “membership interest” is, unless otherwise provided in a nonstock corporation’s certificate of incorporation, a member’s share of the profits and losses of a nonstock corporation, or a member’s right to receive distributions of the nonstock corporation’s assets, or both;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(d)(2) (src:210)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a member's share of the profits and losses of the nonstock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a member's right to receive distributions of the nonstock corporation's assets` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 114(d)(2) the interest of the member is a membership interest` `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise` `it is a member's share of the profits and losses of the nonstock corporation` `it is a member's right to receive distributions of the nonstock corporation's assets` MEANS
        (NOT (`the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise`))
    AND (   `it is a member's share of the profits and losses of the nonstock corporation`
         OR `it is a member's right to receive distributions of the nonstock corporation's assets`)

-- A "nonprofit nonstock corporation" is a nonstock corporation that does not have membership interests.
-- src:211 | (3) A “nonprofit nonstock corporation” is a nonstock corporation that does not have membership interests; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(d)(3) (src:211)
GIVEN `the corporation is a nonstock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has membership interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 114(d)(3) the corporation is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` `the corporation is a nonstock corporation` `the corporation has membership interests` MEANS
        `the corporation is a nonstock corporation`
    AND (NOT (`the corporation has membership interests`))

-- A "charitable nonstock corporation" is any nonprofit nonstock corporation that is exempt from taxation under
-- section 501(c)(3) of the United States Internal Revenue Code, or any successor provisions (federal law, an input).
-- src:209 | (1) A “charitable nonstock corporation” is any nonprofit nonstock corporation that is exempt from taxation under § 501(c)(3) of the United States Internal Revenue Code [26 U.S.C. § 501(c)(3)], or any successor provisions.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(d)(1) (src:209)
GIVEN `the corporation is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is exempt from taxation under § 501(c)(3) of the United States Internal Revenue Code, or any successor provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 114(d)(1) the corporation is a charitable nonstock corporation` `the corporation is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` `the corporation is exempt from taxation under § 501(c)(3) of the United States Internal Revenue Code, or any successor provisions` MEANS
        `the corporation is a nonprofit nonstock corporation`
    AND `the corporation is exempt from taxation under § 501(c)(3) of the United States Internal Revenue Code, or any successor provisions`

-- The four kinds the core names, decided from the four facts. A corporation not organized under this chapter is not
-- covered (NOTHING).
-- src:209 | (1) A “charitable nonstock corporation” is any nonprofit nonstock corporation that is exempt from taxation under § 501(c)(3) of the United States Internal Revenue Code [26 U.S.C. § 501(c)(3)], or any successor provisions.
-- src:210 | (2) A “membership interest” is, unless otherwise provided in a nonstock corporation’s certificate of incorporation, a member’s share of the profits and losses of a nonstock corporation, or a member’s right to receive distributions of the nonstock corporation’s assets, or both;
-- src:211 | (3) A “nonprofit nonstock corporation” is a nonstock corporation that does not have membership interests; and
-- src:212 | (4) A “nonstock corporation” is any corporation organized under this chapter that is not authorized to issue capital stock.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(d)(1) to (4) (src:209-212)
GIVEN `the corporation is organized under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is authorized to issue capital stock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has membership interests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is exempt from taxation under § 501(c)(3) of the United States Internal Revenue Code, or any successor provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Kind of corporation`
`s 114(d) the kind of the corporation` `the corporation is organized under this chapter` `the corporation is authorized to issue capital stock` `the corporation has membership interests` `the corporation is exempt from taxation under § 501(c)(3) of the United States Internal Revenue Code, or any successor provisions` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the corporation is organized under this chapter`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the corporation is authorized to issue capital stock`
         THEN JUST `a stock corporation`
         ELSE IF `the corporation has membership interests`
              THEN JUST `a nonstock corporation with membership interests`
              ELSE IF `the corporation is exempt from taxation under § 501(c)(3) of the United States Internal Revenue Code, or any successor provisions`
                   THEN JUST `a charitable nonstock corporation`
                   ELSE JUST `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable`
